1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,450
We'll use a decision matrix to map out a couple of

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:07,095
the different ideas that we've been discussing for the grocery store scenario.

3
00:00:07,095 --> 00:00:11,730
Looking at a decision matrix in terms of user value versus effort,

4
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:14,835
we'll plot those ideas onto this chart.

5
00:00:14,835 --> 00:00:17,130
One idea that we've discussed is

6
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:21,030
navigation inside a store based on a user's shopping list.

7
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:23,205
In terms of user value,

8
00:00:23,205 --> 00:00:25,320
there's some user value there.

9
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,940
But generally store layouts don't change frequently,

10
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,110
and once a user knows where an item is

11
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:34,440
it's likely it's going to continue to stay in that same spot.

12
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:36,345
In terms of effort,

13
00:00:36,345 --> 00:00:39,725
this isn't really the simplest thing to build for a couple of reasons.

14
00:00:39,725 --> 00:00:41,945
Each store has a different layout.

15
00:00:41,945 --> 00:00:47,705
So we would need the ability to track location of items on a per store basis,

16
00:00:47,705 --> 00:00:49,265
and the other challenge is that

17
00:00:49,265 --> 00:00:53,525
indoor positioning can be really difficult to do accurately.

18
00:00:53,525 --> 00:00:55,910
This would make it challenging for us to know

19
00:00:55,910 --> 00:00:58,715
where a user is actually located in the store,

20
00:00:58,715 --> 00:01:00,350
and if we don't know this,

21
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:03,005
how are we going to be able to provide navigation?

22
00:01:03,005 --> 00:01:07,895
So I would put this idea in the low value high effort quadrant.

23
00:01:07,895 --> 00:01:11,420
Another idea was recommended or

24
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:15,155
suggested items based on the other items that you have in the cart.

25
00:01:15,155 --> 00:01:17,015
In terms of user value,

26
00:01:17,015 --> 00:01:18,980
there's definitely some user value here.

27
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:21,200
Suggested products can make it easier

28
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,675
for users to find products that they're interested in.

29
00:01:23,675 --> 00:01:25,490
In terms of effort,

30
00:01:25,490 --> 00:01:28,370
it should be relatively straightforward to recommend items

31
00:01:28,370 --> 00:01:31,670
based on purchase patterns across the entire user base.

32
00:01:31,670 --> 00:01:36,575
For example, users who bought this product also bought this product.

33
00:01:36,575 --> 00:01:39,530
I would put this idea just on the edge of

34
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:43,595
high user value and between low and medium effort,

35
00:01:43,595 --> 00:01:50,195
and the last idea that we're going to go through was the concept of auto pilot.

36
00:01:50,195 --> 00:01:52,130
In terms of user value,

37
00:01:52,130 --> 00:01:55,370
we think that there's value in this idea because it saves

38
00:01:55,370 --> 00:01:59,500
people time from managing and tracking items that need to be purchased.

39
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:04,520
We also think there's value in terms of giving users the flexibility of how often

40
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:07,355
automatic purchases happen as well as

41
00:02:07,355 --> 00:02:11,525
the option for in-store pickup versus delivery direct to home.

42
00:02:11,525 --> 00:02:13,160
In terms of effort,

43
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:18,215
this idea require lot of effort for two main pieces of complexity.

44
00:02:18,215 --> 00:02:22,105
First, we would have to figure out how to build a subscription functionality,

45
00:02:22,105 --> 00:02:25,595
and because we're offering multiple fulfillment methods,

46
00:02:25,595 --> 00:02:28,220
we need to make sure that we have processes in place for

47
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:31,400
both in-store pickup and delivery to home.

48
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:37,730
So I would put this idea as high user value and a little more than medium effort.

49
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:43,310
So looking at all of our ideas plotted out on the decision matrix,

50
00:02:43,310 --> 00:02:47,270
we can see that navigate requires a lot of effort,

51
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:49,370
but provides low user value.

52
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:54,890
Suggested products provides a decent amount of user value and not a ton of effort,

53
00:02:54,890 --> 00:02:58,850
and autopilot provides the most user value,

54
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:02,330
but also requires a decent amount of effort.

55
00:03:02,330 --> 00:03:08,360
So keeping in mind that low value high effort ideas usually don't pan out,

56
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:11,030
it's not worth pursuing navigate.

57
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:16,700
Suggested products has some user value and is relatively low effort.

58
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,505
So it does make sense to pursue this at some point.

59
00:03:19,505 --> 00:03:26,030
Autopilot has much more user value and will require even more effort to build.

60
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:29,495
But we really do think there's something there to this autopilot idea.

61
00:03:29,495 --> 00:03:32,220
So we're going to pursue it further.

